1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,732
Outlook was down for about a day.

2
00:00:02,912 --> 00:00:04,563
And it wasn't a hack.

3
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:05,966
On November 12,

4
00:00:05,966 --> 00:00:09,109
Microsoft's email servers started failing their

5
00:00:09,109 --> 00:00:11,651
own safety checks and dropped offline.

6
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:15,103
The rest got overloaded and failed too.

7
00:00:15,283 --> 00:00:16,925
Outlook and Teams went

8
00:00:16,925 --> 00:00:18,567
down around the world.

9
00:00:18,747 --> 00:00:21,966
Microsoft hasn't published the full cause yet.

10
00:00:22,366 --> 00:00:23,122
Next time,

11
00:00:23,122 --> 00:00:25,842
check Microsoft's status page first.

12
00:00:26,022 --> 00:00:28,345
Expect late emails.

13
00:00:28,525 --> 00:00:30,327
Move anything urgent to

14
00:00:30,327 --> 00:00:31,816
a call or WhatsApp.

15
00:00:32,216 --> 00:00:33,821
Should you switch to Google?

16
00:00:34,001 --> 00:00:34,675
You can,

17
00:00:34,675 --> 00:00:36,784
but Google goes down too,

18
00:00:36,784 --> 00:00:39,651
and moving a company is expensive.

19
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:42,338
A backup plan costs far less.

20
00:00:42,738 --> 00:00:45,113
You can't stop Microsoft from breaking,

21
00:00:45,113 --> 00:00:47,489
but you can keep your business running.

22
00:00:47,669 --> 00:00:49,542
Pick a second channel,

23
00:00:49,542 --> 00:00:51,756
keep key contacts offline,

24
00:00:51,756 --> 00:00:53,544
and practise it once.

25
00:00:53,944 --> 00:00:55,411
What did your office do

26
00:00:55,411 --> 00:00:56,878
when Outlook went down?
